        "original_id": "3a6acd3b-2421-5e6a-9f76-6f130be0cd93",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Philadelphus, Sarracenia, mock orange\n- Concepts: plant genera, species counts, native ranges, common names\n\nFacts:\n- Philadelphus is a genus of about 60 species of shrubs that typically grow from 3 to 20 feet (1 to 6 meters) tall.\n- Philadelphus is native to North America, Central America, Asia, and locally to southeast Europe.\n- Sarracenia is a North American genus of pitcher plants that comprises 8 to 11 species and is commonly called trumpet pitchers.\n- Mock orange or mock-orange typically refers to Philadelphus, a mostly Holarctic genus of shrubs.\n- Mock orange particularly refers to Philadelphus coronarius, which is widely cultivated as an ornamental.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
